     ssiizzee — display object file segment sizes (text, data and bss)

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ssiizzee [--ttww] [_f_i_l_e _._._.]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ssiizzee displays the text, data and bss segment sizes of the specified
     _f_i_l_e_(_s_) in bytes (in decimal), and the sum of the three segments (in dec‐
     imal and hexadecimal).  If a library (archive) is given, ssiizzee displays
     the segment sizes for each object archive member.  If no _f_i_l_e is speci‐
     fied, ssiizzee attempts to report on the file _a_._o_u_t.

     The options are as follows:

     --tt      At the end of the output print a total of the sizes of all the
             object files processed.

     --ww      Warn about non-object archive members.  Normally, ssiizzee will
             silently ignore all archive members which are not object files.

